integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ WithTokenStoreCallTimeout ~ added ~ keep ~ bounds one round trip of every token store door; measured on a live redis with gated replies, a write waited the client's five-second ceiling and a read was retried for good on a context without deadline, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ ./cache.RegisterBackendServiceWithOptions ~ added ~ keep ~ the door through which a composition root hands WithCommandTimeout to the backend registered in the container, which nothing could pass before; the option-less door is unchanged, and v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ ./cache.ModuleConfig.BackendOptions ~ added ~ keep ~ hands the same backend options through the module, the way the parent package's ModuleConfig.TokenStoreOptions has since its first tag; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ LockerOption ~ added ~ keep ~ the option type of the redis locker, the shape every other client-backed service of this package configures through; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ WithLockerCallTimeout ~ added ~ keep ~ bounds one round trip of Acquire, Release and Refresh; measured on a live redis with gated replies, each Lua script on a request without deadline waited the client's five-second ceiling, and the framework's RunExclusive campaigns on that context; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ NewLockerWithOptions ~ added ~ keep ~ the door that takes LockerOption; NewLocker keeps its signature, since a variadic parameter added to it would be a signature change, and builds the same locker at the defaults; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ RegisterLockerServiceWithOptions ~ added ~ keep ~ the door through which a composition root hands WithLockerCallTimeout to the locker registered in the container, the shape of cache.RegisterBackendServiceWithOptions; the option-less door is unchanged; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ ModuleConfig.LockerOptions ~ added ~ keep ~ hands the same locker options through the module, the way TokenStoreOptions has since the first tag and cache.ModuleConfig.BackendOptions does; the struct was already non-comparable through TokenStoreOptions; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ NonceGuardOption ~ added ~ keep ~ the option type of the redis nonce guard, which had none: NewNonceGuardWithPrefix was its only configuration; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ WithNonceGuardCallTimeout ~ added ~ keep ~ bounds one round trip of Remember; measured on a live redis with gated replies, the Lua record on a request without deadline waited the client's five-second ceiling and the read-only EXISTS of a non-positive ttl had not returned after fifteen seconds, the client retrying it for as long as the context allows; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ WithNonceGuardKeyPrefix ~ added ~ keep ~ the prefix as an option beside the call timeout, so a guard built through NewNonceGuardWithOptions can carry both; NewNonceGuardWithPrefix keeps its signature and calls it; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ compatible ~ NewNonceGuardWithOptions ~ added ~ keep ~ the door that takes NonceGuardOption; NewNonceGuard and NewNonceGuardWithPrefix keep their signatures and build the same guard; v3.14.0 is the last minor that ships features
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ incompatible ~ ./cache.ModuleConfig ~ old is comparable, new is not ~ keep ~ the slice field BackendOptions makes the config non-comparable, the shape the parent package's ModuleConfig has carried since its first tag through TokenStoreOptions; measured, nothing in the tree compares a module config, and a composition root builds it once to hand it to NewModule by value
integrations/rueidis/v3 ~ incompatible ~ ./cache.Module ~ old is comparable, new is not ~ keep ~ the module holds its config by value, so it follows ModuleConfig out of comparability, the shape the parent package's Module has carried since its first tag; the application keys its registered-module set on the Module interface, whose dynamic value is the *Module pointer NewModule answers — a Module value cannot satisfy the interface, its methods take a pointer — so the key stays hashable
